  "title": "30003952: accepted exact smooth braid lifts of prescribed Dehn twists",
  "body": "## Complete smooth construction\n\nFor any prescribed essential pair meeting once on an oriented smooth surface,\nactual orientation-preserving C\u221e diffeomorphisms A,B represent the prescribed\nright Dehn-twist classes and satisfy ABA = BAB as maps. The construction gives\nC\u221e inverses, compact support inside a regular neighborhood and identity on a\nboundary collar. It answers the original homeomorphism, C1 and every finite Cr\nquestions affirmatively, including the negative-Euler-characteristic cases.\n\nThe result lifts the specified homomorphism B3\u2192Mod(S); it need not be a section\nof its image when ambient relations are added. The full proof and mathematical\naudit preserve this earlier required scope correction, consistent handedness\nand source inverse-matrix evidence, global flow commutation, exact unit boundary\nwinding, and the zero-central-offset proof. No new mathematical correction is\nintroduced in this edition.\n\nMann\u2013Tshishiku, Theorem 4.1, already proves smooth B3 realization on a disk with\nthree marked points. This directly relevant positive prior work is prominently\ncredited. No novelty or priority is claimed:\nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/1802.00490\nOriginal question: A\u2019Campo, Problem 9, Oberwolfach Report 40/2018, p. 2527:\nhttps://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2018/40\n\n## Distribution and review limits\n\nExactly eight authored proof/audit/acceptance/status/source-review or public\nverification-metadata files are added under\n`unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30003952/`.\nThe audit records 28 independent exact checks in each of normal and optimized\nPython, plus 10 algebraic and 10 integrity defects rejected in each mode.\nThese historical checks supplement the analytic proof; they do not replace\nits global smoothness, topology, commutation or gluing arguments.\n\nThis AI-assisted manuscript and audit are unrefereed. Acceptance is not external\nhuman peer review, journal acceptance or proof-assistant certification. No\nfull higher-genus mapping-class-group realization, convention-free nonorientable\nstatement, exhaustive literature coverage or priority certification is claimed.\n\nThe proof requires no omitted executable or raw output. Programs, raw outputs,\ngenerated datasets, copied third-party source documents/text/images and private\ncoordination material are excluded. Edition preparation rechecked frozen byte\nidentities and publication integrity, without new scholarly retrieval, source-text\ninspection, literature search or rerunning original mathematical programs.\nQUEUE.md and unrelated repository content remain unchanged. No merge, release,\nDOI, journal submission or external outreach is requested.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.json`: 3,736 bytes; SHA-256 `c99e31eef616129ca930db8bda33d163927b656ac48784f76e963b8118be1e12`.\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,592 bytes; SHA-256 `3f32a2690acf50a7c6730c28d129ee2899574eaa8f43cbab473944943604f42c`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_AUDIT.md`: 16,880 bytes; SHA-256 `a4112206ff8b997531a08f040a4a113ec0dd7cba829459e943599e842880c51e`.\n- `PROOF.md`: 16,909 bytes; SHA-256 `f00fb3ff79fbbe02b35c62ff8269d4bd49a01120e980bfc8ea33361fd6cca16d`.\n- `README.md`: 3,415 bytes; SHA-256 `9e11e7b26560acdcc9a5fd1f093c03dae442b8f5d95da65c88ff23ca87b78680`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 10,291 bytes; SHA-256 `42d866d4c7a74ae63ec3d6f60abe828b85d204948045f19e64d6c1221f2a3364`.\n- `SOURCE_REVIEW.md`: 5,733 bytes; SHA-256 `90f8c24c5de795c9d896c172e96c5fe6dcbebab9f8cd2c4b70bbd0ab0e3beaf0`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 2,914 bytes; SHA-256 `740d68952f4d25b64c75c8b0fa39776ab2653b14f65ee8866bf4a3ebb51f6bd9`.\n\nThe manifest lists eight members and hashes the other seven; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
